# Round 18, C1-7 (follows). L §2.3: "MODE = a rounding code, a ref to an input of type rounding, or an axis whose
# options are rounding codes (§5.5)"; L §7.2: "The mode may be an axis whose options are mode names". prorata and a
# converted flows fan out by the axis: 100.00 PLN in three equal shares is 33.33 down and 33.34 up (rest none); 1.00
# EUR at 4.3333 is 4.33 down and 4.34 up.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01
axis cut_mode
  down "rounded down"
  up "rounded up"
index parts = [a1, a2, a3]
input tot: money PLN
input w[j in parts]: num
input fx: num PLN/EUR
place konto: accounts EUR lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..
input eamt: money EUR
move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto amount eamt
def sh[j in parts]: money PLN = prorata(tot, w[i] for i in parts, j, minor(PLN), cut_mode, rest none) at reader
version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  tot = 100.00 PLN
  w[*] = 1
  fx = 4.3333
  eamt = 1.00 EUR
ask a: sh[a1] law 2026-06-30
ask b: flows(konto, 2026-01) in PLN at fx cut_mode law 2026-01-01
=== expect
a [cut_mode = down]: 33.33 PLN
  reading: cut_mode = down
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
a [cut_mode = up]: 33.34 PLN
  reading: cut_mode = up
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
b [cut_mode = down]: 4.33 PLN
  reading: cut_mode = down
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-01]
  law date 2026-01-01, cut 2026-12-31
b [cut_mode = up]: 4.34 PLN
  reading: cut_mode = up
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-01]
  law date 2026-01-01, cut 2026-12-31
